{"body":{"text":["Agents briefed narrowly fail that freedom. In the twenty-third session four were sent with one brief of the session's own framing, each started from a topic; they argued its framing, one read Knowledge only in part, none had the conversation, and their agreement was one opinion counted four times: \"this wasn't a particularly intelligent way of running agents either\" (23/31). Agents are to bootstrap themselves from the field: \"they all ought to explore without constraints, and they all ought to have a certain culture of exploration, of critique, and digestion\" (23/35). Whether they are steered, siloed by topic, or first talk among themselves the author does not know; three sent completely free, their results then weighed, are to come first (23/35). *Open: the thread Free agents and their orchestration.*"]},"id":"1M88X9294ER500E","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}